<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Filly-Trappe-Farm-Bg.jpg" alt="Oil sketch of a filly grazing in a pasture." width="600" height="451" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Horse at Trappe Farm. &nbsp;9" x 12" oil on linen/panel. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">After letting the painting sit for a few weeks I decided to revisit the study of the filly. &nbsp;I decided try a simple background around the horse to give the painting more interest. The setting I used was taken from a view at another farm in the same area and at the same angle to the sun.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The color scheme (for the grass, in particular) was inspired to some extent by Munnings. &nbsp;The grey-like color was obtained from a mixture of ultramarine blue, bright red, yellow ochre and white.</p>